        "b2000002-0000-4000-8000-0000000000ff": {
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\n- Appmixer account: auth+hubspot@appmixer.com (service appmixer:hubspot), HubSpot portal 148964607 (developer test account).\n- The HubSpot app's webhook target URL must point at this Appmixer instance (own app, appId + apiKey in the service config) — the trigger subscribes to `e2e_watched_deal_note` itself at flow start and re-activates the default deal subscriptions.\n- **Custom deal property `e2e_watched_deal_note` must exist** (string/text, group dealinformation). Create it once: HubSpot MakeApiCall `POST /crm/v3/properties/deals` `{\"name\":\"e2e_watched_deal_note\",\"label\":\"E2E Watched Deal Note\",\"type\":\"string\",\"fieldType\":\"text\",\"groupName\":\"dealinformation\"}`.\n- Negative step: the first update changes `amount` (NOT watched) — the trigger must stay silent; the Assert expects the custom value AND amount 250, so an emission from the amount change or from the creation events fails it.\n- The Waits must stay (subscription propagation, create → update → update → cleanup spacing).",
